The plain-text alternative of the fixed-width fixture.

The HTML part is a 600px table with no media queries at all, which is the half
of real mail that cannot adapt itself to a narrow pane.

--alt-0011
Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

<html>
  <head>
    <title>Fixed-width newsletter</title>
  </head>
  <body style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#eeeeee;">
    <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background:#eeeeee;">
      <tr>
        <td align="center" style="padding:20px;">
          <table width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"
                 style="width:600px;background:#ffffff;font-family:Georgia,serif;">
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:24px;">
                <h1 style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:26px;color:#16598d;">A column pinned to 600px</h1>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;">
                  Nothing in this message adapts. There is no viewport tag, no
                  <code>&#64;media</code> block and no percentage width anywhere inside the
                  container: the table is 600 pixels wide in the markup and again in its inline
                  style, which is how a great deal of real mail is still authored.
                </p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;">
                  A reading pane narrower than 600px therefore has nothing to work with. The
                  contract's answer is to scale the whole page down until it fits rather than let
                  this sentence run off the right edge, and to leave the reader a pinch to get
                  back in. See docs/reading-zoom.md.
                </p>
                <table width="552" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"
                       style="width:552px;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;">
                  <tr>
                    <td style="border:1px solid #d9d9d9;padding:8px;width:184px;">First column</td>
                    <td style="border:1px solid #d9d9d9;padding:8px;width:184px;">Second column</td>
                    <td style="border:1px solid #d9d9d9;padding:8px;width:184px;">Third column</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td style="border:1px solid #d9d9d9;padding:8px;">A fixed cell</td>
                    <td style="border:1px solid #d9d9d9;padding:8px;">Another fixed cell</td>
                    <td style="border:1px solid #d9d9d9;padding:8px;">The rightmost cell</td>
                  </tr>
                </table>
              </td>
            </tr>
          </table>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </body>
</html>

--alt-0011--
